    [Doc]Use PCP8 DP2 for A3 DSpark prefill with Model Runner V2 (#19257)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Port the final documentation changes from #19201 (`releases/v0.30.0`) to
    `main`.
    
    Update the A3 DeepSeek-V4-Flash DSpark Prefill example to PCP8 / DP2 /
    TP1. Extend the launcher to allocate TP × PCP devices per DP rank,
    enable Model Runner V2 on both DSpark nodes, and declare the matching
    Prefill DP/TP/PCP topology in both Mooncake configurations.
    
    Prefill uses 16384 batched tokens, memory utilization 0.94,
    `enable_fused_mc2: 1`, and prefix caching with retention interval 4096.
    Decode keeps 480 batched tokens and uses `FULL_DECODE_ONLY` without
    fixed capture sizes or draft `enforce_eager`. Document the V2
    configuration in the parameter descriptions. MTP and A2 deployment
    examples retain their existing configuration.
    
    Also synchronize the review follow-ups from #19201: use the existing
    model tutorial format to state that support is largely feature-complete
    from v0.26.0 and this guide is validated and written based on v0.30.0,
    recommend the latest release candidate or official version for new
    features, fill the DSpark checkpoint hardware requirements, and use
    Atlas 800I A2/A3 names throughout.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation only; no runtime code changes. No release note fragment is
    required.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Markdownlint passed for the modified document using the repository
    configuration.
    - Verified the synchronized version paragraph and hardware requirements
    match the final source PR, and the review follow-ups do not change any
    fenced code blocks.
    - `git diff --cached --check` passed.
    - Parsed the embedded A3 Python launcher, checked all A3 shell blocks
    with `bash -n`, and parsed their JSON configuration.
    - Verified the entire A3 PD section exactly matches the final source PR
    and the MTP templates remain unchanged from `main`.
    - Full `bash format.sh ci` could not complete: actionlint's Go
    dependencies timed out downloading from proxy.golang.org. Markdownlint
    and focused document checks passed separately.
    - No NPU serving/inference run was performed. Static checks do not
    establish runtime correctness.
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [ ] Boundary / edge-case coverage: no runtime code change; launcher
    grouping checks were performed for the source PR.
    - [ ] Regression test: documentation-only update.
    - [ ] Error / failure path coverage: no runtime code change.
    - [ ] Meaningful & reliable tests: syntax, JSON and source-port checks
    described above.
    - [ ] Performance impact: no runtime implementation change; no benchmark
    claim.
    
